Specification Advanced Define 

# Define 
# | Name      | Value | Notes                 |
# | HIGH_DATA | 100   | Highest allowed input |
# | LOW_DATA  | 1     | Lowest allowed input  |

Define LOW_DATA = 1
Define HIGH_DATA = 100
Scenario  Simple Replacement
Given this data : IDValue
| ID | Value      |
| A  | =HIGH_DATA |
| B  | =LOW_DATA  |
Then should be equal to data : IDValue
| ID | Value |
| A  | 100   |
| B  | 1     |

#Define 
#| Name          | Value                    | Notes                            |
#| AVERAGE_VALUE | (LOW_DATA + HIGH_DATA)/2 | will be passed at "(1 + 100)/2)" |

Define AVERAGE_VALUE = 50
Scenario:  Try out replacements with a calculation
Given this data: IDValue
| ID | Value          |
| A  | =HIGH_DATA     |
| B  | =LOW_DATA      |
| C  | =AVERAGE_VALUE |
Then should be equhal to data: IDValue
| ID | Value |
| A  | 100   |
| B  | 1     |
| C  | 50    |

Attributes IDValue 
Description for testing 
| Name  | Datatype | Default |
| ID    | String   |         |
| Value | String   |         |

Scenario Define with a Table 
Given this data: IDValue
=EQUAL_DATA
Then should be equhal to data: IDValue
| ID | Value |
| A  | 100   |
| B  | 1     |
| C  | 50    |

Define EQUAL_DATA = 
| ID | Value |
| A  | 100   |
| B  | 1     |
| C  | 50    |



